run_accession	study_accession	secondary_study_accession	sample_accession	experiment_accession	scientific_name	sample_title	sample_description	experiment_title	library_strategy	library_source	library_selection	library_layout	instrument_platform	instrument_model	library_construction_protocol	read_count	base_count	fastq_ftp	fastq_md5	fastq_bytes
SRR10022302	PRJNA561657	SRP219298	SAMN12623600	SRX6759363	Mus musculus	GFP-(ESC) Mid Repli-seq rep2	GFP-(ESC) Mid Repli-seq rep2	NextSeq 500 sequencing: GSM4042924: GFP-(ESC) Mid Repli-seq rep2 Mus musculus OTHER	OTHER	GENOMIC	other	SINGLE	ILLUMINA	NextSeq 500	Cells were pulse labeled with the nucleotide analog 5-bromo-2-deoxyuridine (BrdU) for 2 h to mark nascent DNA. The cells were sorted into early-, mid- and late S-phase fractions 20,000 cells each on the basis of DNA content using FACS. Genomic DNA was isolated from each fraction using SDS-proteinase K buffer and purified by phenol-chloroform extraction. Genomic DNA was fragmented using the Covaris sonicator to get 700 bp average fragment size. The sheared BrdU-labeled DNA from each fraction was immunoprecipitated using 0.5 μg of mouse anti-BrdU antibody followed by 50 μL of precleared-Dynabeads sheep anti-mouse IgG (Invitrogen, 11201D). The immunoprecipitated pellet was digested overnight with Proteinase K and purified by phenol-chloroform extraction. The replication timing libraries were prepared based on Accel-NGS methyl seq library kit (Swift Biosciences, MI, USA) according to the manufacturer's protocol. The BrDU immuno-precipitated DNA was denatured and subjected to Adaptase reaction. This step was followed by an extension reaction with two cleanup steps utilizing Agencourt Ampure XP beads (Beckman Coulter, IN, USA). The elute was subjected to ligation step with a follow-up of Ampure bead mediated purification. Indexing PCR was done with appropriate and unique adaptor primer for an individual sample preparation. PCR program consisted of 98ºC for 30 seconds, then 9 cycles of 98ºC for 10 seconds, 60ºC for 30 seconds and 60ºC for 60 seconds followed by a 4ºC hold cycle. The PCR product was further purified by Ampure beads and eluted out in a 20μl volume using TE buffer provided by the manufacturer. The libraries were checked for size, using Agilent 2200 Tape Station (Agilent, CA, USA) utilizing DNA high sensitivity tape (Agilent, CA, USA). Up to 12 libraries were pooled together after Qubit quantification with Qubit DNA HS assay kit (Thermofisher Scientific, NY, USA) and loaded into Nextseq 500/550 high output cartridge (Illumina, CA, USA) for 75 cycle single end sequencing.	68863939	5195855753	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR100/002/SRR10022302/SRR10022302.fastq.gz	59975b25489cf8661ab3b3ec795ceb4e	2767409820
